From 2a301fc1f3a3136115e90d79d0a1cb70ddb378ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:57:46 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 24/80] EXPERIMENT: precise invalidation for Mono call-target
 patches (MACRUNNER_FEX_MONO_BP_PRECISE)

Mono's backpatcher rewrites the 8-byte imm64 of `mov r11, imm64; call/jmp r11`
(49 BB <imm64> 41 FF D3/E3). MonoBackpatcherWrite invalidated the whole
4 KiB page (every translation touching it) and every thread whose L1/L2 held a
block of that page zeroed its 4 MiB call-return stack under the exclusive code
lock. On Hollow Knight that is ~17 000 page drops and call-return clears until
the main menu (~1.2 s of thread time) and ~29 000 re-translations of unchanged
neighbours.

With the gate, every translation also records its guest byte extent
[DecodedMinAddress, DecodedMaxAddress) per code page. A patch whose surrounding
bytes match the call-target pattern drops only the entry points whose recorded
extent overlaps the 8 patched bytes (entry points without a record are dropped
as before), clears only those entries from each thread's L1/L2, and leaves the
call-return stacks alone: an old translation differs only in the call target,
so returning into it calls the old target (Mono's trampoline), which is what a
core that has not yet observed the cross-modification would do. Any other
backpatcher write keeps the old path. Counters: bp_precise, bp_precise_erased,
bp_fallback in the macrunner-fex-jit line.

Svod-Origin: exp-inv-20260929 3dd87a06e (0037 of fexbuild-0019s)
Svod-Note: reordered before 0020-0035: no HB_SCOPE span in InvalidateCallTargetPatch (added with the HB_SPANS patch), the capture gate list entry moves to the capture patch
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
